    "body": "While I'm here, want to note -- the `ignoreCase` option has the potential to be an obstacle to the cases which can't handle regexp groups, but I think it's actually fine because I think the match algorithm ends up making everything ASCII. Otherwise, the fact that `vi` regexps do Unicode case folding (so k could match not only uppercase K but also kelvin symbol K , for instance) would be a potential issue for implementations that implemented matching without a regexp engine.",
